      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10647333::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf treatment will transform single-phase BCC NbMoTaW into a dual-phase material containing discrete precipitates in a continuous BCC matrix.",
      "field": "hypothesis; structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10647333::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-rich precipitates may be a B2 or another ordered intermetallic phase.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Trace Hf locally changes NbMoTaW thermodynamics so as to promote secondary-phase precipitation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10647333::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fine Hf-rich precipitates can deflect cracks at room temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fine Hf-rich precipitates can enhance dislocation mobility at room temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf modification will significantly increase room-temperature plastic strain before fracture relative to untreated NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10647333::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The dominant refractory BCC matrix will preserve comparable yield strength at 1600 °C after Hf modification.",
      "field": "mechanism; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10453588::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-modified alloy will maintain the irradiation resistance of untreated NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The refractory BCC matrix provides defect-tolerant behavior under irradiation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
